## DEFINITION
ERRAT is a protein structure validation tool that evaluates the quality of a 3D protein model by analyzing non-bonded atomic interactions.

## PURPOSE
- Assess the quality of protein structures.
- Identify regions with structural errors.
- Validate predicted protein models.
- Improve model reliability before further analysis.

## KEY METRIC
- **Overall Quality Factor:** Indicates the overall accuracy of the protein structure. Higher values represent better-quality models
(generally >90% for high-resolution structures).

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- PDB (.pdb) protein structure file.

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Used after protein structure prediction or modeling.
- Detects regions with abnormal atomic interactions.
- Generates a quality score and error plot.
- Commonly used alongside other validation tools such as PROCHECK and Verify3D.
